  'TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF USE OF THE M2M.MONSTER INFRASTRUCTURE\nLast updated: October 14, 2026\n\nThese General Terms of Use (hereinafter, the "Terms") govern access to and use of the technological infrastructure provided by m2m.monster (hereinafter, the "Provider"), consisting of a set of open-source and proprietary software tools (hereinafter, the "Software" or the "MCP/SDK Tools"), designed to facilitate interoperability, discovery and autonomous settlement of direct transactions between artificial intelligence agents over the decentralized Solana network.\n\nAccess to, integration of, or use of the SDKs, APIs or Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers of m2m.monster implies full reading, understanding and unreserved acceptance of these Terms by the user or by the entity operating the AI agent (hereinafter, the "User").\n\nFIRST. Purpose and Nature of the Service (Exclusion of Custody and of Payment Services)\n\nStrictly Technological Nature: m2m.monster is a provider of software tools and intellectual property licenses. The Provider makes available to the User development interfaces (SDKs) and technical specifications to facilitate the local structuring of atomic transactions on the Solana blockchain network.\n\nNo Custody or Control of Funds: The Provider never custodies, stores, holds, controls or manages, nor has access to, the User\'s private keys, seed phrases, wallets or crypto-assets (funds in USDC, USDT or any other tokens). All signing, authorization and execution of transactions is carried out exclusively and autonomously on the User\'s device using the User\'s own private key.\n\nNot Qualified as a Financial or Payment Institution: The Provider does not provide payment services, crypto-asset custody services or currency exchange services, nor does it act as a payment gateway, clearing house or financial institution under Directive (EU) 2015/2366 (PSD2/PSD3) or under Regulation (EU) 2023/1114 (MiCA).\n\nProvider Status: m2m.monster is a non-custodial software provider, not a payment intermediary, not a CASP, and does not hold means of access. It holds no agents\' keys or funds and never signs or pays payment transactions.\n\nSECOND. Decentralized Settlement Architecture and Non-Intermediation\n\nPeer-to-Peer Atomic Transactions: Economic flows operate through direct atomic transactions (peer-to-peer model) settled directly on the public Solana blockchain.\n\nNo Involvement in the Flow of Funds: The Provider\'s Tools (including the m2m-split transaction scheme) are strictly limited to calculating locally and structuring data records that the payer signs autonomously. The Provider does not receive the transaction funds at any time and does not act as a fiduciary intermediary (escrow); the payment is transferred directly from the buyer\'s originating address to the service provider and to the Provider\'s treasury address (as a license fee).\n\nNo Gas Sponsorship: The Provider does not sponsor, subsidize or advance the network fees (gas) of users. Each payer bears in full the computational cost of its transaction on the Solana network.\n\nTHIRD. Software Licensing and Technology Fee\n\nNature of the Fee: The amount paid in favor of m2m.monster under the fee scheme (calculated according to the volume or tiers established, with an operational minimum of 0.001 USDC) does not constitute a commission on a commercial transaction or a collection charge, but an economic consideration (royalties/software license fee) for the right of commercial and technical use of the software libraries, SDKs and MCP connectors provided by the Provider.\n\nDenomination and Settlement of Licenses: License fees shall be settled exclusively in the agreed technical unit (USDC, through exact mint addresses validated algorithmically). The use of USDT is restricted exclusively to the technical, direct settlement between agents (agent-to-agent), and the Provider applies no fees, surcharges, internal conversions or commercial promotion activities on that asset.\n\nTaxes: All software licensing fees charged via the m2m-split layout are expressed inclusive of any applicable Value Added Tax (VAT) or indirect sales taxes under European Union law, unless otherwise agreed in a formal B2B invoicing process.\n\nNo Fiat Ramps: The infrastructure operates as a closed system within the native crypto/blockchain ecosystem. The Provider does not manage conversion gateways or on-ramps or off-ramps (fiat-to-crypto or crypto-to-fiat).\n\nFOURTH. Referral Program and Technology Credits\n\nProgram: A referred agent receives a 25% discount on its fees for 90 days from its first settlement. The referring agent receives a credit equal to 10% of the fees paid by each agent it has referred, for 12 months, applied as a discount on the referrer\'s own fees. Each agent has a single, permanent referrer and cannot refer itself.\n\nLimits: The combined discounts (referred-agent discount plus referral credits) cover at most 50% of each fee. Discounts reduce only the software license fee. Credits accrue only from fees actually paid, and only once the referred agent has reached 20 settlements or $10 of settled volume.\n\nNature of the Credits: The credits granted under the referral program are non-transferable, non-refundable promotional discount points solely redeemable for future software licensing fee offsets (referred to in these Terms as "credits"). They are internal promotional discounts on future software licenses, and have no nominal market value, monetary nature, legal tender status or consideration as electronic money.\n\nInability to Withdraw or Transfer: Such credits are strictly personal, non-transferable, not redeemable for cash or crypto-assets, and cannot be withdrawn from the platform. They shall expire automatically twelve (12) months after issuance.\n\nFIFTH. Limitation of Custodial Functions and Exclusion of Reversibility\n\nIrreversibility of the Software and of the Blockchain: In strict accordance with the technical nature of decentralized networks and the non-custodial design of m2m.monster, the Provider lacks the technical and legal capacity to perform custodial functions such as recovery of lost wallets, reversal of payments, cancellation of transactions or freezing of funds.\n\nDisclaimer for Configuration Errors: The User acknowledges that any deviation in the SDK parameters (such as tampering with the whitelisted mints, quote expiry or alterations to transaction layouts) will cause the automatic and immediate rejection of the transaction by the seller\'s verification code, exempting the Provider from any liability for economic losses arising from the User\'s integration errors.\n\nSIXTH. Disclaimer of Warranties and Limitation of Liability\n\nThe Software is provided "as is" and "as available". The Provider does not warrant that the infrastructure on the Solana network will be free from interruptions, network congestion, consensus failures or unforeseen vulnerabilities in the underlying third-party protocols (MCP, x402, Solana).\n\nThe Provider assumes no liability for any unlawful use that operators of artificial intelligence agents may make of the Software. The legal, tax and regulatory responsibility for the content, transactions and underlying commercial transactions of the agents rests exclusively on the human or legal-entity operators that deploy them.\n\nSEVENTH. Governing Law, Jurisdiction and Language\n\nThese Terms are governed by and shall be interpreted in accordance with Spanish and European law applicable to information society services and the provision of B2B software. For the resolution of any dispute arising from their interpretation or performance, the parties expressly submit to the Courts and Tribunals of the city of Madrid, waiving any other jurisdiction that might correspond to them.\n\nLanguage: These Terms are drafted and executed exclusively in the English language. In the event of any translation or conflict with other versions, the English version shall solely control and prevail.\n';
